  "title": "Distinguished Lecture Series",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Main article",
      "text": "The D-MAVT Distinguished Lecture Series brings world leading scientists and engineers to ETH Zurich to present their work in a colloquium and to meet with its faculty and students. The colloquium has broad attendance by faculty, staff, Master and Doctoral students from all departments of ETH Zurich.\n\nThis year’s topics are:\n\nPiezoelectric micromachined ultrasonic transducers in consumer electronics\n\nProf. David A. Horsley, University of California\n\n17 October 2016 from 5.15 p.m. in HG F30\n\nFlying Carpets: Ultralight Structures for Space Solar Power\n\nProf. Sergio Pellegrino , California Institute of Technology\n\n14 November 2016 from 5:15 p.m. in HG F30"
    }
  ],
